## Why This Is Asked
Tests a practical tree DP approach: building a connected component of fixed size while propagating choices up a rooted tree, including reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Tree knapsack DP for connected subgraphs
- Subtree containment and topmost node principle
- Reconstruction via parent/child pointers
- Time/space: O(N*K^2) in naive merge, with optimizations possible

## Code Example
```javascript
function dfs(u, p) {
  dp[u] = new Array(size[u] + 1).fill(-Infinity);
  dp[u][1] = val[u];
  for (const v of g[u]) if (v !== p) {
    dfs(v, u);
    // merge dp[u] with bestChild from v
    const ndp = new Array(size[u] + size[v] + 1).fill(-Infinity);
    for (let a = 1; a <= size[u]; a++) {
      if (dp[u][a] === -Infinity) continue;
      // option: take nothing from v
      ndp[a] = Math.max(ndp[a], dp[u][a]);
      for (let b = 1; b <= size[v]; b++) {
        if (best[v][b] === -Infinity) continue;
        ndp[a + b] = Math.max(ndp[a + b], dp[u][a] + best[v][b]);
      }
    }
    size[u] += size[v];
    dp[u] = ndp;
  }
}
```

